1
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,283
Welcome to the Watermill Inn.

2
00:00:08,283 --> 00:00:09,000
Oh, Richard,

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,500
it's exactly as it was when we were married!

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,400
And when I got married.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,800
Even the old patchwork quilt is the same!

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,700
My great-grandmother made that quilt

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,300
when Teddy Roosevelt was President.

8
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,700
In those days, when they made quilts.

9
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,600
they cut patches

10
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,900
so that each one would be a part of it.

11
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,100
What a lovely tradition!

12
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,200
Thank you for calling us.

13
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,400
I remember you and your wife

14
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,400
We were very young.

15
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,700
And very much in love.

16
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:43,900
We have a baby now.

17
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:48,000
How wonderful! A boy or a girl?

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,100
A boy--Max.

19
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,784
Do you have a picture?

20
00:00:51,784 --> 00:00:57,700
Would a professional photographer be without a picture?

21
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:00,500
Oh, he's adorable!

22
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,700
And very bright.

23
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,600
Like his father. A real Stewart.

24
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,200
And very good-looking, like his mother.

25
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,346
Well, it's nice to have you with us again.

26
00:01:08,346 --> 00:01:10,700
Next time, bring the baby.

27
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:12,861
You see, Richard? Max is welcome here.

28
00:01:12,861 --> 00:01:14,200
Not on our anniversary.

29
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,400
This vacation is for you and me.

30
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,500
If there's anything you need, please call me.

31
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,200
I'll be in the front office all day.

32
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:32,800
Oh, I took the liberty of ordering some breakfast for you.

33
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:50,600
Just put it over there, Charles.

34
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:54,100
Thank you, Charles.

35
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,600
Compliments of the Watermill Inn.

36
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,200
Thank you.

37
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:02,500
Thank you so much.

38
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,212
Now, this is my idea of a good time.

39
00:02:06,212 --> 00:02:13,600
Let's see ... hotcakes and maple syrup, with scrambled eggs.

40
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:17,400
Umm ... smell that coffee ... cinnamon and cloves.

41
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,400
Homemade buttermilk biscuits.

42
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:23,300
Slices of orange with burnt honey.

43
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,900
Let's eat!

44
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:26,100
First I want to call home

45
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:27,600
and check on your mother and the baby.

46
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,200
Honey, if there were any problems,

47
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,500
she would call us.

48
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,600
She doesn't know we've changed hotels.

49
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:42,400
You're right. Of course.

50
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,300
Hello, operator.

51
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:52,900
I'd like to call Riverdale, New York.

52
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:56,400
This food is heavenly, isn't it?

53
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:07,400
This whole place is heavenly.

54
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:11,200
Do you remember that old desk?

55
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:13,100
Mrs. Montefiore told me that

56
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,000
George Washington sat at that desk

57
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,800
and wrote to his wife Martha.

58
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:20,400
What do you want to do after breakfast?

59
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:23,200
Why don't we take a walk down to the river?

60
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,400
In the rain?

61
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:32,800
No. Look out the window. The sun is shining!

62
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,800
Now this is my idea of a good time!
